"play_h": "Play",
"play": "<p>The game is in <strong>early alpha</strong> (version 0.7.0). <strong>Windows</strong>: download the latest version from the <a href=\"https://github.com/BigFatDeuce/A-Survivor-to-the-Past/releases/latest\" rel=\"noopener\">Releases page</a>, extract the whole zip and launch <code>A Survivor to the Past.exe</code>. Windows may warn that the game is not signed: click <em>More info</em> → <em>Run anyway</em>. <strong>Linux, macOS and handhelds</strong> (PortMaster, experimental): same page, take the zip for your system and follow its <code>README.txt</code>. The game then <strong>updates itself</strong>: at launch it checks GitHub for a new version, downloads it in the background and installs it at the next launch (Options → Updates: Automatic / Ask me / Off). Your settings are kept and no personal data is sent: updates only contact GitHub, and the world leaderboard only contacts the game's website when you open it or publish a score (nickname and score).</p>",
